{"type":"standard","title":"Darin LaHood","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Darin LaHood</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q5222780","titles":{"canonical":"Darin_LaHood","normalized":"Darin LaHood","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Darin LaHood</span></span>"},"pageid":31031169,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Darin_LaHood_official_photo.jpg/330px-Darin_LaHood_official_photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":495},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/21/Darin_LaHood_official_photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":999,"height":1500},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1378384011","tid":"74872889-bfbb-11f1-9632-2fb8987f884f","timestamp":"2026-10-04T06:18:46Z","description":"American politician (born 1968)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darin_LaHood","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darin_LaHood?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darin_LaHood?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Darin_LaHood"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darin_LaHood","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Darin_LaHood","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darin_LaHood?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Darin_LaHood"}},"extract":"Darin McKay LaHood is an American attorney and politician who has served as a U.S. representative from Illinois since 2015. A member of the Republican Party, LaHood has represented the 16th district since 2023, and previously represented the 18th district from 2015 to 2023, a district which was once represented by House Minority Leader Robert H. Michel. The son of Republican Ray LaHood, who represented this district from 1995 until 2009, previously served in the Illinois Senate from the 37th legislative district from 2011 to 2015, before being elected to Congress in a special election following the resignation of Aaron Schock.","extract_html":"<p><b>Darin McKay LaHood</b> is an American attorney and politician who has served as a U.S. representative from Illinois since 2015. A member of the Republican Party, LaHood has represented the 16th district since 2023, and previously represented the 18th district from 2015 to 2023, a district which was once represented by House Minority Leader Robert H. Michel. The son of Republican Ray LaHood, who represented this district from 1995 until 2009, previously served in the Illinois Senate from the 37th legislative district from 2011 to 2015, before being elected to Congress in a special election following the resignation of Aaron Schock.</p>"}